Kyno

Kyno is a mini monolithic kernel licensed under BSD, designed to run on BIOS systems with support for both 32-bit and 64-bit architectures.
It includes:

    Kyboot: bootloader written in Assembly.

    Kyno: the monolithic kernel written in C.

    Kynner: process scheduler.

    FAT32: integrated filesystem support.

  Philosophy

    Minimalism: a small, educational kernel.

    Open Source BSD: free, flexible, and community-driven.

    Compatibility: runs on BIOS, supports 32-bit and 64-bit CPUs.

    Community: forums and developer platform for drivers, themes, and apps.

